* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)pə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[usurp]]s.
#: {{syn|en|usurpator}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Martin Gayford|title=There's more to Ming than a vase &#91;print version: 16 August 2014, pp.&nbsp;R6–R7&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/art/art-features/11040914/Theres-more-to-Ming-than-a-vase.html|work={{w|The Daily Telegraph}} (Review)|date=15 September 2014|passage=The fact that the [[w:Yongle Emperor|Yongle emperor]] was therefore a '''usurper''', regicide and nepoticide (nephew-killer) made compiling the Veritable Record&nbsp;– or official history&nbsp;– of his reign a most dangerous scholarly post. The official given this ticklish task managed to survive several drafts, finally producing one that pleased his master as it omitted the dead nephew's reign altogether.}}

